The TypeScript scanner and scheduler use bounded input buffers and header/CRC
descriptors. The caller supplies packet payload I/O. The metadata reader handles STREAMINFO
and block descriptors; trusted handlers supply remaining payload validation.
FFmpeg is a development reference, not a runtime dependency. Full AVIO scheduling,
container timestamps, malformed diagnostics, decoding and CLI compatibility
remain separate requirements. Package-level redistribution and project-wide
license review remain open.

